{"parentUuid":"421c3c49-bf2b-4ff7-8c54-7dd6692f7dac","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"18312b63-252f-49f8-a02f-218b82ecc330","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PouJr61FuJKeQzdC9eP1Vo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the bugs found, ordered by severity:\n\n---\n\n**1. `tour_tui.go`, lines 1996-2004 — Medium — Off-by-one in `clearTourInlineView` / guard check after computation**\n\n```go\nlineCount := strings.Count(view, \"\\n\") + 1\nif view == \"\" {\n    return\n}\n```\n\nThe empty-string guard comes *after* the `lineCount` computation. That's harmless for correctness (lineCount would be 1, the loop would emit one spurious clear-line escape), but it's also not the only issue: when `view` is non-empty, `lineCount = strings.Count(view, \"\\n\") + 1` over-counts by one when the view string itself ends with a newline (the common case for `strings.Join`-built views). A view with 3 lines ending in `\\n` has 3 newlines, giving `lineCount = 4` — one extra ANSI clear-line escape is emitted, wiping a line of content above the spinner. The guard should come first and lineCount should not add 1 when the string ends with a newline.\n\n**2. `tour/state.go`, line 1527 — Medium — V2 checkpoint store constructed with hardcoded `\"origin\"` remote**\n\n```go\nv2Infos, err := checkpoint.NewV2GitStore(repo, \"origin\").ListCommitted(ctx)\n```\n\nThe remote name `\"origin\"` is hardcoded. Repos that don't have an `\"origin\"` remote (e.g., users who renamed it to `upstream` or `github`) will always get a false `false` from the v2 check — the v2 checkpoint branch will simply not be found. This degrades their stage from `StageWorkflow` to `StageFirstCapture`, showing them the \"no history yet\" tail even when they have extensive checkpoint history. The correct approach is to resolve the configured or default remote name from settings/git config rather than hardcoding `\"origin\"`.\n\n**3. `tour/blog.go`, line 361 — Medium — HTTP response body read when status is non-OK, plus body never closed on non-200 path**\n\nActually the `defer resp.Body.Close()` is placed before the status check, so the body *is* closed on non-200 — that part is correct. But the non-200 path returns an error that includes only `resp.Status` and not the body, which is benign. No bug here.\n\n**4. `tour/prompt.go`, `escapeForTags` replacement string — Medium — Backslash in replacement can be misinterpreted by `regexp.ReplaceAll`**\n\n```go\nreturn closingTagPattern.ReplaceAll(stripInvisibles(payload), []byte(\"<\\\\/$1>\"))\n```\n\nIn Go's `regexp` package, the replacement string for `ReplaceAll` uses `$` for group references but backslash `\\` has no special meaning in the *replacement* argument (unlike PCRE). The literal bytes `<\\/` followed by `$1` and `>` will be emitted literally — the `\\` character will appear in the output: `<\\/state>`, `<\\/post>`, etc. The tests confirm this is *intentional* (the test cases assert `\"<\\\\/state>\"` which in a Go string literal is `<\\/state>`), so the tests pass. This is working as designed, not a bug.\n\n**5. `tour_tui.go`, line 1989-1993 — Medium — Goroutine accesses `m.ctx` and `m.run` without synchronization; `m.ctx` is nil at `Init()` time**\n\n```go\nfunc (m tourStatusModel) runGenerate() tea.Cmd {\n    return func() tea.Msg {\n        result, err := m.run(m.ctx)\n```\n\n`newTourStatusModel` returns a `tourStatusModel` with `ctx` and `cancel` as zero values (`nil`). The caller then sets `model.ctx` and `model.cancel` on the returned struct. However, `Init()` is called by BubbleTea immediately after `NewProgram(model, ...)` and *before* the program has a chance to process any external mutations. In practice `defaultRunTourTUI` sets `model.ctx = runCtx` and `model.cancel = cancel` *before* calling `program.Run()`, so the copy given to `NewProgram` already has them set — Go passes structs by value at the `NewProgram` call. This is fine. No real race here as long as the assignments happen before `program.Run()`.\n\n---\n\n**Summary of real bugs:**\n\n| File | Line(s) | Severity | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour_tui.go` | 1996–2004 | Medium | `clearTourInlineView`: empty-string guard is placed after `lineCount` computation, and `+1` always over-counts lines when the view ends with `\\n` — emits one extra ANSI clear-line escape, potentially wiping a content line above the spinner |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/tour/state.go` | 1527 | Medium | `repoHasHistory` hardcodes `\"origin\"` as the v2 remote name; users with a differently-named remote always get `false` from the v2 store, causing `StageFirstCapture` to be returned even when they have committed checkpoint history on the v2 branch |\n\nNo critical bugs found. The sanitization logic (`escapeForTags`, `stripInvisibles`, `stripControlSequences`) is well-constructed and the HTTP fetch in `blog.go` correctly size-caps the body and defers `Close()` before the status check."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: adb5c5812a76137b4 (use SendMessage with to: 'adb5c5812a76137b4' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 59697\ntool_uses: 6\nduration_ms: 360252</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"6807eba8-c2ee-40be-b7d9-e554ac2eafb7","timestamp":"2026-05-08T20:29:27.641Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are doing a shallow bug-scan of PR #1146 (Add `entire tour` command). Focus only on the diff itself — do not read other files for extra context.\n\n**Diff:** `/tmp/pr1146.diff` (2064 lines)\n**Working dir:** `/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/cli/entire-learn`\n\nRead the diff in full. Look for **large, obvious bugs**:\n- Logic errors (off-by-one, swapped args, wrong comparison)\n- Nil dereferences / index-out-of-range without guards on user-facing paths\n- Goroutine/concurrency issues (data races, unsynchronized state, leaked goroutines)\n- Resource leaks (unclosed files/HTTP bodies, deferred-in-loop patterns)\n- Wrong error handling (swallowed errors that should 