derr()/root.ErrOrStderr() into executeTour/translateTourError) before returning SilentError, or return a non-Silent error so main prints it.\",\"created\":\"2026-05-07T22:56:05Z\",\"line\":173,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"tourNoTextGeneratorMessage says \\\"'entire tour' renders the tour by piping the discovered command surface through your locally-installed agent\\\", but the default `entire tour` path renders embedded markdown and does not require an agent; only `--latest`/`--regenerate` do. This message will be misleading in the error case—consider explicitly referencing those flags and clarifying that the embedded tour works without an agent.\\n\",\"created\":\"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"The loading UI title says \\\"Fetching the latest dispatch\\\", but this command fetches the latest blog post and renders a digest. Using the wrong noun here is confusing for users; consider renaming to something like \\\"Fetching the latest post\\\" / \\\"Generating latest digest\\\" to match `--latest` behavior and other messaging.\\n\",\"created\":\"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"This error wrap says \\\"generate latest dispatch\\\", but this path generates a blog-post digest for `entire tour --latest` rather than a dispatch. Consider renaming the message to reflect the tour/latest digest so errors are easier to understand and grep.\\n\",\"created\":\"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"The comment claims json.Marshal's default escaping would turn \\\"\\u003cid|sha\\u003e\\\" into \\\"\\u003cid|sha\\u003e\\\", but the actual default behavior is to HTML-escape angle brackets (e.g. to \\\\u003c...\\\\u003e). Consider updating the example in this comment to show the real escaped form so future readers understand why SetEscapeHTML(false) matters.\\n\",\"created\":\"2026-05-07T22:56:06Z\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/tour/prompt.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"### Agent output unsanitized in `--latest` path\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\n`GenerateLatest` returns raw agent output without calling `stripControlSequences`, unlike `regenerateFromAgent` which sanitizes its output. When `--latest` and `--regenerate` are both passed, `latestFlag` wins in the `generate` closure but `regenerateFlag` causes the result to be written raw to stdout via `fmt.Fprintln` — bypassing glamour and delivering unsanitized agent output to the persistence path (the mise task pipes stdout to a file). Even without `--regenerate`, the glamour error-fallback path in `executeTour` writes `result.Markdown` directly to the terminal unsanitized.\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: c1691e44-1938-4482-aa8b-79b8cb569867 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\ncmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go#L60-L82\\ncmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go#L137-L141\\nLOCATIONS END --\\u003e\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eAdditional Locations (1)\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n- [`cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go#L137-L141`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/c8ca02ba09a29551dcebbd134cf2d871ffbbd708/cmd/entire/cli/tour_cmd.go#L137-L141)\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Web\\\" width=\\\"99\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/div\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003csup\\u003eReviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c8ca02ba09a29551dcebbd134cf2d871ffbbd708. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).\\u003c/sup\\u003e\\n\",\"created\":\"2026-05-08T01:18:05Z\",\"line\":82,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go\",\"user\":\"cursor[bot]\"}\n{\"body\":\"### Regenerate always resolves StageSetup in CI, breaking regen\\n\\n**High Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nThe `--regenerate` path calls `ResolveState` which checks whether Entire is enabled in the current repo. In CI (and fresh checkouts), no `.entire/settings.json` exists, so `IsSetUpAny` returns `false` and `ResolveState` returns `StageSetup`. The state is then passed to the agent prompt, which instructs the agent to produce a minimal 4–6 line setup guide instead of the full workflow tour. The mise task validation (≥4 `## ` headers) rejects this output, so CI tour regeneration always fails and every release ships the stub. The `--regenerate` path likely needs to force the state to `StageWorkflow` since the embedded tour is only served to workflow/first-capture users.\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 3ac22422-79b4-4746-aaeb-6634c26be41b --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\ncmd/entire/cli/tour/run.go#L91-L103\\ncmd/entir